cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Solar Rhythm: the browser instrument of The 25th Cycle"
abstract: >-
  Browser instrument that turns the daily sunspot record (SILSO, 1818 to today)
  into a drone, percussion, timbre and form for a Eurorack system, through Web
  MIDI and an Expert Sleepers FH-2. A drone runs through every phase of the solar
  cycle; over it, each phase has its own percussion (Crater, Kraken and the hits
  of a Make Noise Strega), whose number of hits and timbre follow the data, each
  voice on its own loop length. Part of the audiovisual piece The 25th Cycle.
